9c0\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"b48a8e8e-f610-4422-acfc-4b9b3fd0ae51\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T01:17:48.231Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011Cgf7W9ZBwkx1YCG4GMRU6\\\",\\\"wire_tool_inputs\\\":{\\\"toolu_01FF8JyFsfhrACJB9GuK1XWv\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /tmp/wire-src/hublib; grep -n \\\\\\\"AIHub\\\\\\\\|<meta\\\\\\\" ghost.html | head -60; cat retrofit.md | head -60\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Read ghost example hub usage\\\"}}}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01FF8JyFsfhrACJB9GuK1XWv\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"4:<meta charset=\\\\\\\"utf-8\\\\\\\">\\\\n5:<meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\\\\\">\\\\n7:<meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"A minimal ghost game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: everyone runs the same seeded course on their own device and sees the others as ghosts.\\\\\\\">\\\\n8:<meta name=\\\\\\\"theme-color\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"#0f1b2e\\\\\\\">\\\\n9:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:type\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Tech demo\\\\\\\">\\\\n10:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:players\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\">\\\\n11:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\">\\\\n12:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-players\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"2-4\\\\\\\">\\\\n13:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-mode\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"ghost\\\\\\\">\\\\n14:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\">\\\\n15:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-goal\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Fastest to the end of the course wins\\\\\\\">\\\\n16:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-howto\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Steer: ← →, A D or a stick · boost: Space or Cross · or drag a finger\\\\\\\">\\\\n25:  if (root.AIHub) return;\\\\n201:    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\\\\n501:  root.AIHub = hub;\\\\n623:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [2, 4] });\\\\n626:  run.rocks = course(AIHub.rng('course'));\\\\n631:  AIHub.ready();\\\\n632:  AIHub.on('start', () => { run.phase = 'racing'; unlockAudio(); });\\\\n633:  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\\\n639:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => ghosts.delete(id));\\\\n640:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => {\\\\n641:    if (run.phase === 'racing') AIHub.result({ score: Math.floor(run.d) });\\\\n643:  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\\\\n666:const raceTime = () => (hub ? AIHub.time() : performance.now() - soloStart);\\\\n691:        AIHub.result({ time: run.finishedAt });\\\\n692:        AIHub.send({ t: 'done', time: run.finishedAt });\\\\n699:    AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: AREA, x: Math.round(run.x), d: Math.round(run.d) }, { reliable: false });\\\\n700:    if (run.phase === 'racing') AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(run.d), label: `${Math.round((run.d / LENGTH) * 100)}% of the course` });\\\\n# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\\\\n\\\\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\\\\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\\\\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\\\\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\\\\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\\\\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\\\\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\\\\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\\\\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\\\\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\\\\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\\\\n\\\\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\\\\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\\\\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\\\\nagainst it:\\\\n\\\\n<protocol>\\\\n{{contract}}\\\\n</protocol>\\\\n\\\\nDo only this:\\\\n\\\\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\\\\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\\\\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\\\\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\\\\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\\\\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\">` with it.\\\\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\\\\n   `<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:webgpu\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\">`.\\\\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\\\\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\\\\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \\\\\\\"press\\\\n   start\\\\\\\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\\\\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\\\\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\\\\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\\\\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\\\\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\\\\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\\\\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\\\\n   still going.\\\\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\\\\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\\\\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\\\\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\\\\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\\\\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\\\\n\\\\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\\\\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\\\\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\\\\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\\\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0fcdb66e-7b81-4152-a7ad-a6f1924439c0\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"9ae15a63-0415-43d5-9fd2-7465b0c30ab5\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T01:17:48.249Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"4:<meta charset=\\\\\\\"utf-8\\\\\\\">\\\\n5:<meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\\\\\">\\\\n7:<meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"A minimal ghost game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: everyone runs the same seeded course on their own device and sees the others as ghosts.\\\\\\\">\\\\n8:<meta name=\\\\\\\"theme-color\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"#0f1b2e\\\\\\\">\\\\n9:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:type\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Tech demo\\\\\\\">\\\\n10:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:players\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\">\\\\n11:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\">\\\\n12:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-players\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"2-4\\\\\\\">\\\\n13:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-mode\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"ghost\\\\\\\">\\\\n14:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\">\\\\n15:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-goal\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Fastest to the end of the course wins\\\\\\\">\\\\n16:<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-howto\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Steer: ← →, A D or a stick · boost: Space or Cross · or drag a finger\\\\\\\">\\\\n25:  if (root.AIHub) return;\\\\n201:    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\\\\n501:  root.AIHub = hub;\\\\n623:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [2, 4] });\\\\n626:  run.rocks = course(AIHub.rng('course'));\\\\n631:  AIHub.ready();\\\\n632:  AIHub.on('start', () => { run.phase = 'racing'; unlockAudio(); });\\\\n633:  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\\\\n639:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => ghosts.delete(id));\\\\n640:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => {\\\\n641:    if (run.phase === 'racing') AIHub.result({ score: Math.floor(run.d) });\\\\n643:  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\\\\n666:const raceTime = () => (hub ? AIHub.time() : performance.now() - soloStart);\\\\n691:        AIHub.result({ time: run.finishedAt });\\\\n692:        AIHub.send({ t: 'done', time: run.finishedAt });\\\\n699:    AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: AREA, x: Math.round(run.x), d: Math.round(run.d) }, { reliable: false });\\\\n700:    if (run.phase === 'racing') AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(run.d), label: `${Math.round((run.d / LENGTH) * 100)}% of the course` });\\\\n# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\\\\n\\\\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\\\\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\\\\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\\\\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\\\\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\\\\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\\\\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\\\\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\\\\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\\\\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\\\\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\\\\n\\\\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\\\\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\\\\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\\\\nagainst it:\\\\n\\\\n<protocol>\\\\n{{contract}}\\\\n</protocol>\\\\n\\\\nDo only this:\\\\n\\\\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\\\\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\\\\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\\\\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\\\\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\\\\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\">` with it.\\\\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\\\\n   `<meta name=\\\\\\\"hub:webgpu\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\">`.\\\\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\\\\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\\\\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \\\\\\\"press\\\\n   start\\\\\\\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\\\\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\\\\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\\\\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\\\\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\\\\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\\\\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\\\\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\\\\n   still going.\\\\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\\\\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\\\\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\\\\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\\\\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\\\\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\\\\n\\\\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\\\\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\\\\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\\\\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01FF8JyFsfhrACJB9GuK1XWv\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":0,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/agent.out\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_016WHueVqNfA4T6ry2yfu7Qn\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"4180323d-f450-4e8c-b0bc-56f3660fbb67\",\"uuid\":\"e00790af-ccd7-4cc0-983d-ad4db4963ab8\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181325__xe8b2f0/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TqTyyFsCbdG1QSrhe9fafU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
