{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D1SsyPz3mitJXBNk3PkUVZ","type":"tool_result","content":"usage: viewport-matrix [-h] [-o OUT] [--engines ENGINES] [--all-engines]\n                       [--only ONLY] [--devices DEVICES] [--full-page]\n                       [--dpr1] [--wait WAIT] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--headed]\n                       url\n\nScreenshot a URL across phone / foldable / tablet / desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox.\n\nWrites one PNG per (device, engine) plus index.html (contact sheet drawn to relative scale) and\nreport.json, and flags horizontal overflow, console errors, page errors and failed requests.\n\nBy default each device runs on the engine it really ships with (iPhone/iPad -> WebKit,\nAndroid -> Chromium) and desktop sizes run on all three engines.\n\n  viewport-matrix http://localhost:5173\n  viewport-matrix http://localhost:5173/play -o /tmp/shots --full-page\n  viewport-matrix URL --engines firefox              # everything in Firefox\n  viewport-matrix URL --all-engines                  # every device x every engine\n  viewport-matrix URL --only phone,foldable --dpr1   # small files, mobile only\n\npositional arguments:\n  url\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help         show this help message and exit\n  -o, --out OUT      output dir (default: $TMPDIR/viewport-matrix/<timestamp>)\n  --engines ENGINES  comma list from chromium,webkit,firefox\n  --all-engines      run every device on every selected engine\n  --only ONLY        comma list of categories: phone,foldable,tablet,desktop\n  --devices DEVICES  comma list of Playwright device names to use instead of\n                     the built-in matrix","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f3c3e9b-9eb4-44c2-94b1-164e7be1aa93","uuid":"ffe45f41-60ea-41c6-93ac-ca8cd52cec1c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:50:58.783Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"usage: viewport-matrix [-h] [-o OUT] [--engines ENGINES] [--all-engines]\n                       [--only ONLY] [--devices DEVICES] [--full-page]\n                       [--dpr1] [--wait WAIT] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--headed]\n                       url\n\nScreenshot a URL across phone / foldable / tablet / desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox.\n\nWrites one PNG per (device, engine) plus index.html (contact sheet drawn to relative scale) and\nreport.json, and flags horizontal overflow, console errors, page errors and failed requests.\n\nBy default each device runs on the engine it really ships with (iPhone/iPad -> WebKit,\nAndroid -> Chromium) and desktop sizes run on all three engines.\n\n  viewport-matrix http://localhost:5173\n  viewport-matrix http://localhost:5173/play -o /tmp/shots --full-page\n  viewport-matrix URL --engines firefox              # everything in Firefox\n  viewport-matrix URL --all-engines                  # every device x every engine\n  viewport-matrix URL --only phone,foldable --dpr1   # small files, mobile only\n\npositional arguments:\n  url\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help         show this help message and exit\n  -o, --out OUT      output dir (default: $TMPDIR/viewport-matrix/<timestamp>)\n  --engines ENGINES  comma list from chromium,webkit,firefox\n  --all-engines      run every device on every selected engine\n  --only ONLY        comma list of categories: phone,foldable,tablet,desktop\n  --devices DEVICES  comma list of Playwright device names to use instead of\n                     the built-in matrix","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":225,"oldLines":3,"newStart":225,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_019ycTDDGLRNkVgmJTnUg3XT\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n}\\n/** ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions): title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory. game.audio.music('adventure') */\\nE.songs = {\\n  title: { bpm: 112, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .16, notes: 'C5 - - - G4 - C5 - E5 - - - D5 - C5 - | D5 - - - G4 - B4 - D5 - - - F5 - E5 - | E5 - - - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - A5 - G5 - | F5 - E5 - D5 - B4 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 | G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 | A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 | F2 - . F2 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . .' },\\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' } ] },\\n  adventure: { bpm: 138, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'pulse', vol: .15, notes: 'E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 B5 - A5 - G5 - E5 - | D5 - E5 - G5 - - A5 G5 - E5 - D5 - . . | E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 D6 - C6 - A5 - G5 - | A5 - G5 - E5 - D5 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/work\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"93b63dd9-a1ff-4df8-b77f-2b0e19e5047c\",\"uuid\":\"6387a727-e08c-465c-9d66-30d15d3da4de\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:50:55.249Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n}\\n/** ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions): title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory. game.audio.music('adventure') */\\nE.songs = {\\n  title: { bpm: 112, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .16, notes: 'C5 - - - G4 - C5 - E5 - - - D5 - C5 - | D5 - - - G4 - B4 - D5 - - - F5 - E5 - | E5 - - - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - A5 - G5 - | F5 - E5 - D5 - B4 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 | G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 | A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 | F2 - . F2 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . .' },\\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' } ] },\\n  adventure: { bpm: 138, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'pulse', vol: .15, notes: 'E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 B5 - A5 - G5 - E5 - | D5 - E5 - G5 - - A5 G5 - E5 - D5 - . . | E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 D6 - C6 - A5 - G5 - | A5 - G5 - E5 - D5 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\",\"stderr\":\"\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/work\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_019ycTDDGLRNkVgmJTnUg3XT\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfA2wVW6GwRC55rMR8gj\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1333,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":130820,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1333,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"93b63dd9-a1ff-4df8-b77f-2b0e19e5047c\",\"uuid\":\"b