ine? Characters with no art files: HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES punches and kicks with real wind-ups, and hitFx gave the brawling a good feel almost for free. The standard pause, settings, rebinding and save screens meant I spent no time on menus.\",","+    \"• Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes, a few times. game.after timers are cleared on a scene change, and that ate the AI Hub ready() call. A mouse move doesn't set input.lastDevice to 'mouse' (only a button does). The pixel font has no middle dot. And I guessed facing and pose values for seated characters ('crouch' stands in for sitting).\",","+    \"• What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The story layer: chapters as steps with check functions, a conversation queue with choices that branch, gibberish voices per speaker, and the two minigames. Also cars drawn from their heading and the gamepad axis inversion.\",","+    \"• What was the hardest part about using the engine? Its size: the API card, the index and the kits are a lot to take in, and the answer is often one line in a 190 KB index. Some behaviour, like timers dying with the scene and the device switching, only shows when you test.\",","+    \"• If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be? I'd overhaul input.lastDevice: it should count mouse movement and stick movement, so prompts follow the device without a game wrapping input.tick.\",","+    \"• If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Built-in axis inversion for both sticks (not just invert aim Y), plus a sit pose and a car or vehicle draw helper for ground views.\"","   ]],","   ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [","-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'","+    \"• What did you like most about this prompt? Clear, testable requirements (attract after 10 s, glyph families, the invert toggles, touch-only behaviour) and the freedom to pick a genre and a voice for the source.\",","+    \"• What was confusing? How Multiplayer should work 'for the game on its own': I read it as local drop-in co-op plus the same Collection round the hub runs. 'Every feature in TASK.md' overlaps with the source's 'all mechanics', which leaves the scope open.\",","+    \"• What was the hardest thing to do? Fitting a whole vertical slice into one session: the story with branching choices, a boss, a car, two minigames, local and online multiplayer, and the attract mode, all tested.\",","+    \"• If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be? A long real-hardware session with a DualSense on a TV, to judge the 10-foot readability and how the controller feels. Automation can only fake the pad.\"","   ]],","   ['CREDITS', [","     'THE BARITONES: design, code, art direction, music, sound and writing by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) in Claude Code.',"]}]}],"moreFiles":3,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/dist/game.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181337__x3ec78e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018hRcvbQ448UVgwsypNPWKp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
