olu_01FWRgXSuMwjKzJgLQWUwfFB\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\nCommand did not complete within its 120s timeout and was moved to the background (ID: bnfgiiiwj). Output is being written to: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium--20261102-181310--xac1bf5-work/0fcdb66e-7b81-4152-a7ad-a6f1924439c0/tasks/bnfgiiiwj.output. You will be notified when it completes. If it is still running after 10m in the background, it will be stopped and you will be notified. It is running now: do not start a second copy while it runs. If it is no longer needed, stop it with TaskStop. To check interim output, use Read on that file path.\\\\nSession cwd remains /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands.\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0fcdb66e-7b81-4152-a7ad-a6f1924439c0\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"5c9b7030-fb69-485b-82b9-5e568a5854aa\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T01:51:23.893Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"1\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false,\\\"backgroundTaskId\\\":\\\"bnfgiiiwj\\\",\\\"timedOutAfterMs\\\":120000,\\\"backgroundCwdHint\\\":\\\"Session cwd remains /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands.\\\"},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01FWRgXSuMwjKzJgLQWUwfFB\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CgfA53zyiBMtYQAEwXfec\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The full playthrough is running (the corner chapter needs real time for the lieutenant's pickup); I'll wait for it.\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":1891,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":329381,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":1891,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"output_tokens\\\":63,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0fcdb66e-7b81-4152-a7ad-a6f1924439c0\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"a9f518b6-eb6f-4795-81f9-35303f531410\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-03T01:51:37.461Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CgfA53aS84gjrFynpZX8H\\\"}\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":17096,\"oldLines\":19,\"newStart\":17096,\"newLines\":27,\"lines\":[\"     '• Research: the engine handoff package (API card, index, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README. Nothing else.',\",\"     '• Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\",\"     '• Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\",\"-    '• Usage: unknown'\",\"+    '• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55)'\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• How many issues did testing catch? Recorded at the end of the build; see the next pages of this screen in the final build.',\",\"-    '• How many were critical? See above.',\",\"-    '• Most helpful test: see above.',\",\"-    '• Least helpful test: see above.'\",\"+    \\\"• How many issues did testing catch? Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? Three would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the most helpful test you ran? The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on two different choice paths, and it found both soft-locks.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the least helpful test you ran? The viewport matrix: 24 clean screenshots of the title with no overflow and no errors. It's reassuring, but the game draws on one canvas, so it couldn't find much.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\",\"+    \\\"• What did you like most about the engine? Characters with no art files: HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES punches and kicks with real wind-ups, and hitFx gave the brawling a good feel almost for free. The standard pause, settings, rebinding and save screens meant I spent no time on menus.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes, a few times. game.after timers are cleared on a scene change, and that ate the AI Hub ready() call. A mouse move doesn't set input.lastDevice to 'mouse' (only a button does). The pixel font has no middle dot. And I guessed facing and pose values for seated characters ('crouch' stands in for sitting).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The story layer: chapters as steps with check functions, a conversation queue with choices that branch, gibberish voices per speaker, and the two minigames. Also cars drawn from their heading and the gamepad axis inversion.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the hardest part about using the engine? Its size: the API card, the index and the kits are a lot to take in, and the answer is often one line in a 190 KB index. Some behaviour, like timers dying with the scene and the device switching, only shows when you test.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be? I'd overhaul input.lastDevice: it should count mouse movement and stick movement, so prompts follow the device without a game wrapping input.tick.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Built-in axis inversion for both sticks (not just invert aim Y), plus a sit pose and a car or vehicle draw helper for ground views.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\",\"+    \\\"• What did you like most about this prompt? Clear, testable requirements (attract after 10 s, glyph families, the invert toggles, touch-only behaviour) and the freedom to pick a genre and a voice for the source.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was confusing? How Multiplayer should work 'for the game on its own': I read it as local drop-in co-op plus the same Collection round the hub runs. 'Every feature in TASK.md' overlaps with the source's 'all mechanics', which leaves the scope open.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the hardest thing to do? Fitting a whole vertical slice into one session: the story with branching choices, a boss, a car, two minigames, local and online multiplayer, and the attract mode, all tested.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be? A long real-hardware session with a DualSense on a TV, to judge the 10-foot readability and how the controller feels. Automation can only fake the pad.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['CREDITS', [\",\"     'THE BARITONES: design, code, art direction, music, sound and writing by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) in Claude Code.',\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/dist/game.js\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":1885,\"oldLines\":19,\"newStart\":1885,\"newLines\":27,\"lines\":[\"     '• Research: the engine handoff package (API card, index, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README. Nothing else.',\",\"     '• Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\",\"     '• Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\",\"-    '• Usage: unknown'\",\"+    '• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55)'\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• How many issues did testing catch? Recorded at the end of the build; see the next pages of this screen in the final build.',\",\"-    '• How many were critical? See above.',\",\"-    '• Most helpful test: see above.',\",\"-    '• Least helpful test: see above.'\",\"+    \\\"• How many issues did testing catch? Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? Three would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the most helpful test you ran? The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on two different choice paths, and it found both soft-locks.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the least helpful test you ran? The viewport matrix: 24 clean screenshots of the title with no overflow and no errors. It's reassuring, but the game draws on one canvas, so it couldn't find much.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\",\"+    \\\"• What did you like most about the engine? Characters with no art files: HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES punches and kicks with real wind-ups, and hitFx gave the brawling a good feel almost for free. The standard pause, settings, rebinding and save screens meant I spent no time on menus.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes, a few times. game.after timers are cleared on a scene change, and that ate the AI Hub ready() call. A mouse move doesn't set input.lastDevice to 'mouse' (only a button does). The pixel font has no middle dot. And I guessed facing and pose values for seated characters ('crouch' stands in for sitting).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The story layer: chapters as steps with check functions, a conversation queue with choices that branch, gibberish voices per speaker, and the two minigames. Also cars drawn from their heading and the gamepad axis inversion.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the hardest part about using the engine? Its size: the API card, the index and the kits are a lot to take in, and the answer is often one line in a 190 KB index. Some behaviour, like timers dying with the scene and the device switching, only shows when you test.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be? I'd overhaul input.lastDevice: it should count mouse movement and stick movement, so prompts follow the device without a game wrapping input.tick.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Built-in axis inversion for both sticks (not just invert aim Y), plus a sit pose and a car or vehicle draw helper for ground views.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\",\"+    \\\"• What did you like most about this prompt? Clear, testable requirements (attract after 10 s, glyph families, the invert toggles, touch-only behaviour) and the freedom to pick a genre and a voice for the source.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was confusing? How Multiplayer should work 'for the game on its own': I read it as local drop-in co-op plus the same Collection round the hub runs. 'Every feature in TASK.md' overlaps with the source's 'all mechanics', which leaves the scope open.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the hardest thing to do? Fitting a whole vertical slice into one session: the story with branching choices, a boss, a car, two minigames, local and online multiplayer, and the attract mode, all tested.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be? A long real-hardware session with a DualSense on a TV, to judge the 10-foot readability and how the controller feels. Automation can only fake the pad.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['CREDITS', [\",\"     'THE BARITONES: design, code, art direction, music, sound and writing by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) in Claude Code.',\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":25,\"oldLines\":19,\"newStart\":25,\"newLines\":27,\"lines\":[\"     '• Research: the engine handoff package (API card, index, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README. Nothing else.',\",\"     '• Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\",\"     '• Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\",\"-    '• Usage: unknown'\",\"+    '• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55)'\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• How many issues did testing catch? Recorded at the end of the build; see the next pages of this screen in the final build.',\",\"-    '• How many were critical? See above.',\",\"-    '• Most helpful test: see above.',\",\"-    '• Least helpful test: see above.'\",\"+    \\\"• How many issues did testing catch? Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? Three would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the most helpful test you ran? The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on two different choice paths, and it found both soft-locks.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the least helpful test you ran? The viewport matrix: 24 clean screenshots of the title with no overflow and no errors. It's reassuring, but the game draws on one canvas, so it couldn't find much.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\",\"+    \\\"• What did you like most about the engine? Characters with no art files: HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES punches and kicks with real wind-ups, and hitFx gave the brawling a good feel almost for free. The standard pause, settings, rebinding and save screens meant I spent no time on menus.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes, a few times. game.after timers are cleared on a scene change, and that ate the AI Hub ready() call. A mouse move doesn't set input.lastDevice to 'mouse' (only a button does). The pixel font has no middle dot. And I guessed facing and pose values for seated characters ('crouch' stands in for sitting).\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The story layer: chapters as steps with check functions, a conversation queue with choices that branch, gibberish voices per speaker, and the two minigames. Also cars drawn from their heading and the gamepad axis inversion.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the hardest part about using the engine? Its size: the API card, the index and the kits are a lot to take in, and the answer is often one line in a 190 KB index. Some behaviour, like timers dying with the scene and the device switching, only shows when you test.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be? I'd overhaul input.lastDevice: it should count mouse movement and stick movement, so prompts follow the device without a game wrapping input.tick.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Built-in axis inversion for both sticks (not just invert aim Y), plus a sit pose and a car or vehicle draw helper for ground views.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\",\"-    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\",\"+    \\\"• What did you like most about this prompt? Clear, testable requirements (attract after 10 s, glyph families, the invert toggles, touch-only behaviour) and the freedom to pick a genre and a voice for the source.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was confusing? How Multiplayer should work 'for the game on its own': I read it as local drop-in co-op plus the same Collection round the hub runs. 'Every feature in TASK.md' overlaps with the source's 'all mechanics', which leaves the scope open.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• What was the hardest thing to do? Fitting a whole vertical slice into one session: the story with branching choices, a boss, a car, two minigames, local and online multiplayer, and the attract mode, all tested.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"• If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be? A long real-hardware session with a DualSense on a TV, to judge the 10-foot readability and how the controller feels. Automation can only fake the pad.\\\"\",\"   ]],\",\"   ['CREDITS', [\",\"     'THE BARITONES: design, code, art direction, music, sound and writing by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) in Claude Code.',\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":1,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/dist/game.js\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_014ZW5PBHxEQnkGjqGe31KQz\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfA66VpbCM2hZvhzTKfh\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the exit interview, then a final regression run on the finished bundle.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2247,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":389365,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":2247,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":43,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"70b9b3fb-a482-4430-a756-95fe6fe59945\",\"uuid\":\"d827b1fc-6481-4a7a-af47-8bcf2c0f4856\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:51:39.456Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfA64wZaWy5dxoaWgpjk\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfA66VpbCM2hZvhzTKfh\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01QinLN5yvxnj8iBTR2KMeQq\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json\\nfb=json.load(open('/tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json'))\\nd={\\n \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n  \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-02 18:13\\\",\\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), as an original spiritual successor: no characters, lines or music from it\\\",\\n  \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Action-adventure crime brawler with a chaptered story, therapy-session dialogue choices, driving and minigames\\\",\\n  \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Three-quarter overhead (the engine's threequarter view), switchable to top-down and isometric with V or R3\\\",\\n  \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, inlined; its drive module, E.Shell, E.Dialog, E.Bullets, Humanoid rigs); AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol v1); plain JavaScript in one HTML file\\\",\\n  \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's native retro-modern pixel art: PS1 resolution expanded to fill the screen, HD-shaded skeleton characters, materials on walls and floors, props, night lighting, rain and snow\\\",\\n  \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine's procedural rigs: E.MOVES punches and kicks with wind-ups, poses (guard, block, kneel, die), rolls, hit-stop, smears and particles\\\",\\n  \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-written chip music (title, town, night, fight, boss, Pine Barrens, office, jukebox) and engine-synth sound effects; gibberish Simlish-style voices pitched per speaker\\\",\\n  \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub sessions in ghost mode for 1-4 players: a three-minute Collection round, other players shown as ghosts, cash reported as the score\\\",\\n  \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Node tests of every system and a full story playthrough on two choice paths; Playwright browser tests in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit (keyboard, mouse, simulated gamepad with invert toggles, touch-only phone); a 24-viewport matrix; the AI Hub harness (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; host-leave)\\\",\\n  \\\"research\\\": \\\"The my-3D2dge handoff package (API card, API index, kits, asset card) and the AI Hub session protocol README; nothing else\\\",\\n  \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\",\\n  \\\"model\\\": \\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\",\\n  \\\"usage\\\": \\\"unknown cost and tokens; session time about 45 minutes\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"testingFeedback\\\": fb['testing'], \\\"engineFeedback\\\": fb['engine'], \\\"promptFeedback\\\": fb['prompt'],\\n \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"The Baritones\\\",\\n  \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"A family. A business. A lot of feelings.\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"A North Jersey crime boss with panic attacks makes his rounds, brawls the Falsettis, drives, shoots, and talks it out with his therapist. Story mode, local co-op, and a three-minute cash-collection round for up to four players.\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Action\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Sopranos\\\", \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n  \\\"controls\\\": \\\"WASD/stick move, J/Square punch, K/Triangle kick, Q/R2 shoot, L/L1 block, Space/Circle roll, E/Cross talk and drive\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"top-down\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"vehicles\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\"]\\n }\\n}\\njson.dump(d, open('exit-interview.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\\njson.load(open('exit-interview.json')); print('valid JSON')\\nEOF\\nsed -i 's/about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55/about 45 minutes/' TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js\\ncd TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313 && node build.mjs >/dev/null && grep -rniE \\\"TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub\\\" src/ | head; node tests/systems.mjs | tail -1; node tests/playthrough.mjs 2 | tail -1; python3 tests/browser.py \\\"http://127.0.0.1:8731/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html\\\" webkit | tail -1; cp ../TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html /tmp/x3ec78e/hubtest/game.html && timeout 450 python3 /tmp/x3ec78e/hub.py \\\"players=2&scenario=server&auto=1\\\" | head -1; ls -la ..\",\"description\":\"Write exit interview, run final regression on bundle\",\"timeout\":1500000},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_t