ected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\","]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":7,"newStart":25,"newLines":7,"lines":["     '• Research: the engine handoff package (API card, index, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README. Nothing else.',","     '• Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',","     '• Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',","-    '• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55)'","+    '• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 45 minutes)'","   ]],","   ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [","     \"• How many issues did testing catch? Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\","]}]}],"moreFiles":24,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/agen