tatus\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"output_file\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Apply the record fix, regenerate, rebuild, verify\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"2e742b85-69f0-4319-abb2-8524df382181\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\\\"}\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":15243,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":15243,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"   \\\"title\\\": \\\"TESTING\\\",\",\"   \\\"lines\\\": [\",\"    \\\"# How many issues did testing catch?\\\",\",\"-   \\\"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\\\",\",\"+   \\\"15 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\\\",\",\"    \\\"# How many were critical / game breaking?\\\",\",\"    \\\"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\\\",\",\"    \\\"# Most helpful test\\\",\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":15243,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":15243,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"   \\\"title\\\": \\\"TESTING\\\",\",\"   \\\"lines\\\": [\",\"    \\\"# How many issues did testing catch?\\\",\",\"-   \\\"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped