\\"title\\\": \\\"TESTING\\\",\",\"   \\\"lines\\\": [\",\"    \\\"# How many issues did testing catch?\\\",\",\"-   \\\"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\\\",\",\"+   \\\"15 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\\\",\",\"    \\\"# How many were critical / game breaking?\\\",\",\"    \\\"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\\\",\",\"    \\\"# Most helpful test\\\",\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/exit-interview.json\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":16,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":16,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"     \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 40 minutes (18:13 to 18:53)\\\"\",\"   },\",\"   \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\",\"-    \\\"14 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\\\",\",\"+    \\\"15 issues. The title screen crashed when the town updated without a hero. Fight waves never advanced because their timer was never counted down. The diner's booth step was never set. A pending fight was dropped on a scene change. Attract mode left the camera in the isometric view. The finale's state leaked into the Collection Run and cut it to black. Tony could not get out of the SUV while it reversed. The touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device. The notice box overflowed on narrow phones. Talk prompts showed during fights. The job log text overlapped its Close prompt. The attract mode's title covered the HUD. The SUV prompt radius was too small. A gamepad's right-stick aim was used as a world direction without converting it from screen space. Hovering the mouse never counted as using the mouse, because the engine only switches to the mouse on a click, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts didn't work until a click.\\\",\",\"     \\\"4 were critical or game-breaking. The title crash broke attract mode. The fight waves never advancing blocked chapter 4. The missing booth step blocked the finale. The finale leaking into the Collection Run ended runs early.\\\",\",\"     \\\"The headless Node test (test.mjs). It plays the whole story through game.debug: the paper, ducks, the car, therapy, breathing, the pork store, three collections, the alley fight, Ma, the yard waves, Ralphie, the diner, the cut to black, then the Collection Run. It caught every blocking bug in seconds.\\\",\",\"     \\\"Setting the stress straight to 100 for a panic screenshot. That skips addStress(), so no panic attack ever started and the picture only showed the RAGE bar.\\\"\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":6,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/src/about.js\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/exit-interview.json\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181319__xb81546/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181328__x694301/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/work/BrewingBad-BreakingBad-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-184349.html\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184349__x8b64cc/work/BrewingBad-BreakingBad-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261102-184349/src/60-start.js\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-185709__x694301/agent.out\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01Pxrqu6nWvYojmDYArUn8Zh\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAcKsKjTDg1nGfpu5nY\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The extra checks found and fixed one more real bug: hovering the mouse didn't count as using it, so hover focus and mouse-button prompts only worked after a click. Every other feature the stop hook questioned now passes a direct check.\\n\\n**New checks** (emulated DualSense in Chromium; iPhone 15 profile in WebKit):\\n\\n| Feature | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| Stick moves Tony; the game switches to the gamepad | pass |\\n| Square = punch; PlayStation symbols by default | pass |\\n| Invert horizontal: stick right moves left | pass |\\n| Invert vertical: stick down moves up | pass |\\n| Xbox symbols option | pass |\\n| Keyboard use switches prompts to keys | pass |\\n| Mouse movement switches prompts to mouse buttons and enables hover focus | **failed, then fixed**, now passes |\\n| Triangle/K on a downed foe stomps | pass |\\n| Touch-only detected; attract mode starts and runs without errors; a tap returns to the title | pass |\\n| Live AI Hub round: each copy receives the other player as a ghost (`ghosts=1` on both) | pass |\\n\\nAfter the fix I rebuilt the single HTML file. On the final file, the headless story test passes and the 4-player lossy-network hub harness still reports **conformance: PASS**. The exit interview now says 15 issues instead of 14 and lists these checks; `exit-interview.json` parses and the in-game About page matches it. A real DualSense, a TV and iOS Safari remain untested.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\\n- **Source:** The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), created by David Chase\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** an action-adventure crime brawler in a small open town (story chapters, melee and a pistol, driving, dialogue choices, stress/panic, FBI heat). Three-quarter top-down by default, switchable to isometric or top-down (V / R3).\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, single file); AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (Protocol v1); vanilla JavaScript, canvas 2D, Web Audio; bundled with Node 24; tested with Playwright 1.63\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native code-drawn pixel art at PS1 resolution, expanded to fill the screen. Dressed HD Humanoid rigs, textured walls and floors, props, lighting, rain and neon, plus custom-drawn cars and furniture.\\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal Humanoid rigs with its built-in attack moves, knock-downs and get-ups; Blob ducks and a pig; scripted cutscenes, tweens and particles.\\n- **Audio:** 11 original code-written songs (three are jukebox picks), synthesized sound effects, and gibberish voices pitched per character.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players (Collection Run, ghosts, progress and result reporting). On its own, the game has local 2-player co-op and no network.\\n- **Testing:**\\n  - headless Node test of the full story plus the Collection Run (all checks pass)\\n  - Chromium and WebKit screenshots\\n  - viewport-matrix: 23 viewports clean\\n  - emulated-DualSense feature checks and touch-only attract mode on an iPhone profile (all pass)\\n  - ghosts received on every copy in a live hub round\\n  - AI Hub harness: PASS with 2 players, with 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and with the host leaving\\n  - nothing tested on a real gamepad, TV or iOS Safari\\n- **Research:** none on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs and the AI Hub README; details of the show come from memory.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown (no usage meter in this session); about 40 minutes to the first finished build (18:13–18:53). The exit interview and About page still give that figure; the follow-up checks took further time that it doesn't count.\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 15:\\n  - the title screen crashed when the town updated with no hero\\n  - fight waves never advanced\\n  - the diner booth step was never set\\n  - a pending fight was lost on a scene change\\n  - attract mode left the camera in isometric view\\n  - the finale's state leaked into the Collection Run\\n  - Tony couldn't get out of the SUV while it was reversing\\n  - the touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device\\n  - the touch-only notice overflowed its box on narrow phones\\n  - talk prompts appeared during fights\\n  - job log text overlapped its Close prompt\\n  - the attract mode's title covered the HUD\\n  - the SUV prompt radius was too small\\n  - gamepad right-stick aim wasn't converted from screen to world direction\\n  - hovering the mouse didn't count as using the mouse until a click\\n- **How many were critical?** 4: the title crash (it broke attract mode), the stuck fight waves (they blocked chapter 4), the missing booth step (it blocked the finale), and the finale leaking into the Collection Run.\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless Node playthrough of the whole story through the game's debug handle. It found every blocking bug within seconds.\\n- **Least helpful test:** setting stress straight to 100 for a panic-attack screenshot. That bypasses the code that starts a panic, so nothing happened.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the standard features I didn't have to build (pause, settings, rebinding, controller symbols, saves, boot screen), the Humanoid rigs with their attack moves, and fixed-step headless testing.\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes:\\n  - the pixel font lacks a check mark, a middle dot and a down triangle\\n  - the \\\"last device\\\" starts as keyboard\\n  - scripts can't wait on promises\\n  - braking the car turns into reversing\\n  - `game.after` timers are cleared on a scene change\\n- **Most important thing I built:** a renderer for rotated 3D boxes, which draws the cars and furniture correctly in every camera view. Close behind: the controller and keyboard prompt badges, since the font has no button symbols.\\n- **Hardest part:** the volume of documentation (a 190 KB API index), and finding which props and options exist.\\n- **Remove or overhaul:** dialogue voices. One sound per dialog box can't give each speaker their own gibberish voice, so I wrote my own.\\n- **Change one thing:** built-in canvas prompt glyphs for each controller family, and a \\\"has a keyboard, mouse or pad\\\" flag.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** a clear checklist of required systems with open creative design, and an exit interview that makes the result easy to audit.\\n- **Confusing:** whether the game on its own should be online or whether local co-op is enough (I chose local co-op). Also, how to write a title with spaces in the file name.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope (a five-chapter slice with combat, driving, heat, stress, saves, attract mode and hub ghost mode), and writing dialogue that sounds like the show without copying it.\\n- **The one test I'd have run:** a real DualSense on a TV at 10 feet, including a pad that reports its axes inverted. Real iOS Safari would be next.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":599,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":358167,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":599,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":777,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\",\"uuid\":\"96699ec6-efd7-4e51-99ec-5211da35c94b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:58:46.821Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAcKPoVfNydCef18XCR\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181319__xb81546/work/BreakingBackyard-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181319.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":16930,"oldLines":7,"newStart":16930,"newLines":7,"lines":["   }"," };"," scenes.town = {","-  pausable: true, view: 'threequarter', touch: [],","+  get pausable() { return !modal; }, view: 'threequarter', touch: [],","   camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1 },","   enter(data = {}) {","     if (data.demo) { savedS = S; S = Object.assign(NEW_STATE(), { ep: 3, step: 1, dirty: 2400, clean: 6000, product: 6, purity: 96.2, flags: { smoke: true, shop: true }, flasks: { fulm: 3, smoke: 3 }, up: { pistol: true }, clock: 17.5, heat: 30, alias: true }); }"]},{"oldStart":16967,"oldLines":7,"newStart":16967,"newLines":7,"lines":["   dra