, asset card) and the AI Hub protocol README and examples. The show's details are from memory\"],[\"Environment\",\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown\"],[\"Model\",\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\"],[\"Usage\",\"Session time about 55 minutes (18:13 to about 19:10); API cost and token counts unknown\"]]},{\"title\":\"TESTING FEEDBACK\",\"rows\":[[\"How many issues did testing catch?\",\"16 issues: a dialog choice that advanced the story twice (skipping a step), story NPCs that were never placed in the world (Vela's office was empty), Escape closing a menu also opening the pause menu, the cook's measure stage waiting forever without input, no guidance when product ran out mid-objective, deep links overridden by the boot screen, touch-only detection failing on WebKit iPhone profiles, a missing font glyph showing as '?', toasts over the HUD, the title tagline over the menu, a patio table on the start spot, the cook's radio covering its gauges, the shop resetting focus after each purchase, buyers spawning too slowly, narrow-screen HUD collisions, and the About page crashing before its data existed.\"],[\"How many were critical / game breaking?\",\"2 were critical: the double-advance after a dialog choice (it silently skipped the Episode 3 sleep step) and the missing NPCs (objectives pointed at empty spots, so the story read as broken).\"],[\"Most helpful test\",\"The real-input browser playthrough: walking by held keys, cooking by timed key presses, fighting with mouse aim and clicks, menus by keys and mouse. It found the Escape/pause conflict, the out-of-product dead end and, through its screenshots, the missing NPCs.\"],[\"Least helpful test\",\"The broad viewport-matrix sweep of the in-game town: all 24 profiles came back clean, and with a pixel-art canvas that scales by itself there was little new for it to find after the first phone screenshot.\"]]},{\"title\":\"ENGINE FEEDBACK\",\"rows\":[[\"What I liked most\",\"Standard features for free: pause menu, settings, rebinding, glyph families, save slots, boot screen, the canvas HUD primitives and E.Dialog with live portraits. Plus a headless engine with exact fixed steps, so the whole story can be played and tested in Node in a couple of seconds.\"],[\"Did I get stuck or guess wrong?\",\"Yes, a few times: the boot sequence overrode a game.go() issued right after game.start() (deep links landed on the title); a Dialog choice closes the box after onChoice, so opening the next line inside onChoice got closed and fired its onDone early; and two players sharing a keyboard silently move player 1 onto F/G/H, which made a prompt test read 'F' instead of 'E'.\"],[\"Most important thing I built\",\"The cook minigame (measure, heat, crystallize, with purity scoring), the DEA patrol loop around E.Suspicion and E.sees (heat, busts, smoke blinding), the 10-foot menus with mouse hover and click, the story/episode event system, the attract-mode demo script, and the AI Hub ghost-mode round.\"],[\"Hardest part\",\"Knowing which calls are safe at which moment in the frame (go() during boot, say() inside dialog callbacks, when pausable is read relative to the scene's update) is not in the API card, so it took testing to find out.\"],[\"What I would remove or overhaul\",\"E.Menu's fixed small type. For a 10-foot, controller-first game I had to write my own menu (bigger rows, a note line, mouse rects); a scale or 'tv' option on E.Menu would remove that duplicate work.\"],[\"What I would change\",\"Document the frame order around scene switches and dialog callbacks (or queue say() calls made from callbacks), and expose a built-in 'invert stick X/Y' controller setting next to invert aim, so games don't have to wrap navigator.getGamepads.\"]]},{\"title\":\"PROMPT FEEDBACK\",\"rows\":[[\"What I liked most\",\"It is concrete about the player's living room: a DualSense at ten feet, glyphs following the last device, a native-feeling mouse, touch-only behaviour, and even the real-world inverted-axis quirk. That made the input and UI goals unambiguous.\"],[\"What was confusing\",\"How much of the source to borrow while staying original (I used original names and riffs on the show's beats), whether 'every feature' includes multiplayer story co-op or only hub support, and the Usage line, since the session cannot see its own token counts.\"],[\"The hardest thing\",\"Scope: five episodes of story, a minigame, stealth, combat, two bosses, attract mode, local co-op and hub multiplayer in one session, all of it tested, without leaving stubs anywhere.\"],[\"The one test I wish I could run\",\"A real controller on a real TV (DualSense over Bluetooth in Chrome and Safari), to verify the glyphs, the stick inversion toggles and the rumble on actual hardware instead of a fake gamepad object.\"]]},{\"title\":\"HOW TO PLAY\",\"rows\":[[\"Goal\",\"Five episodes. Cook in the RV, sell to buyers on the corners, launder dirty cash at the car wash, buy upgrades from Lenny, and survive what comes for you.\"],[\"Controller\",\"Left stick move, right stick aim, Cross interact, Square or R2 punch/shoot, R1 throw flask, Triangle switch flask, Circle roll, L2/L3 sprint, Create ledger, R3 camera, Options pause.\"],[\"Keyboard and mouse\",\"WASD move, mouse aims, E interact, left click punch/shoot (or click a person or door to walk there and use it), right click or G throw, Q switch flask, Space roll, Shift sprint, Tab ledger, V camera, Esc pause.\"],[\"The DEA\",\"Agents see in a cone. Holding product or carrying heat makes them suspicious. Break line of sight, sprint, wait for night, or blind them with smoke. Caught means busted.\"],[\"Two players\",\"Press Start on a second controller, or 2 on the keyboard, to play as Dusty.\"],[\"Settings\",\"Button prompts (PlayStation or Xbox), invert stick horizontal and vertical, difficulty, sight cones, hints, plus the engine's sound, display and comfort options.\"]]},{\"title\":\"CREDITS\",\"rows\":[[\"Game\",\"Breaking Backyard, an original spiritual successor to Breaking Bad (2008-2013). Characters, names and story are original riffs; no affiliation with the show.\"],[\"Made by\",\"Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium) in Claude Code.\"],[\"Engine\",\"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato.\"],[\"Online\",\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.3.0.\"],[\"Music, sound, voices\",\"Written in code: chip-synth songs, synthesized effects, gibberish voices.\"]]}];\n(end scan)\nall 46 checks passed\nall 75 checks passed\nok   players=2&auto=1\nok   players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1\nok   players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave\nok   players=1&auto=1\nhubcheck exit: 0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-185845__x22cc1b/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":575,"oldLines":3,"newStart":575,"newLines":20,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1000,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":300,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"82a0c905-0d33-43fc-af3e-2674c89c7b4b\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":350,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"488b832a-e497-4641-b6c6-95d16aba4465\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1500,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"139b568a-24c8-4f9c-ada5-20f2148016d9\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"df18d03e-d863-4927-85ab-32ee71c39115\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"0a5d6436-2ede-4c22-9fca-aaa2e316830f\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfBgnkKLR5CL1JaB11yv\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1408,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":233462,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1408,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"97237c7a-ee42-4a08-a011-a86c04b1b538\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T02:12:47.563Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfBgnMWVwbQYF9uZqGvx\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":11212,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfBgnkKLR5CL1JaB11yv\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The phone title is fixed: the tagline wraps and sits clear of the menu. Remaining work: fill the feedback sections in About and in the exit interview, rebuild, re-run the checks, and stop the test server.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1408,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":233462,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1408,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4accd60f-1720-4154-a575-c0b8f1413e9f\",\"uuid\":\"2b0ea256-e580-4ec2-8d2a-dea3d5e0c446\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T02:12:47.749Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfBgnMWVwbQYF9uZqGvx\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfBgnkKLR5CL1JaB11yv\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_013Vep5AGWf9ycPDzeXcGKgd\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-185845__x22cc1b/work/WireOnTheCorner-TheWire-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261102-185845 && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\\nimport json\\nTEST = [\\n \\\"Nine issues: two critical (the hero's rig was never created, so every shift crashed on its first step; the hub ready() call was not made after connect, so no round could start), and seven minor layout and flow problems (title overlap, tagline overflow, an unsupported glyph, results alignment, About footer overlap, and a scene-switch race in attract).\\\",\\n \\\"Two: the hero rig crash and the missing hub ready call. Both would have stopped every shift or every hub round.\\\",\\n \\\"The scripted full playthrough, which walks the real systems in order (pickups, pole tuning, witness and lieutenant choices, banking) and reads the outcome back, plus the AI Hub harness run.\\\",\\n \\\"The 10-second attract idle check mostly confirmed a timer. The viewport screenshots only capture the title screen, so they were weaker than a per-scene capture would have been.\\\",\\n]\\nENG = [\\n \\\"The threequarter TileMap, the Humanoid rigs, and the Dialog, Menu and Shell screens gave a readable game quickly; the standard pause, settings and controls screens came for free.\\\",\\n \\\"Wrong guesses: a scene switch changes sceneName before enter() runs, because of the fade, so state from the old scene can briefly be live; the font has no middle dot; and a Dialog choice can only be answered through input, so I added a handle to answer it from code.\\\",\\n \\\"The shift state machine: the clock, heat and burns, the pole tuning mini-game, the conversations with their outcomes, the attract AI, and the hub reporting.\\\",\\n \\\"Working out the return shapes of calls (mouseGround, FlowField.dir, centre helpers) without reading the 1.2 MB source, and the timing of scene transitions.\\\",\\n \\\"The scene switch: the name changes before the new scene's enter() runs. A switch should only change the name once the new scene is entered.\\\",\\n \\\"Let a Dialog's choice be answered by code (a select call), so scripts, tests and tools can drive conversations.\\\",\\n]\\nPROMPT = [\\n \\\"The explicit checklists: the controls, the invert toggles, the touch-only notice, the hub tags and the About content are all concrete enough to build against.\\\",\\n \\\"The About requirement asks for the feedback sections, but they can only be written after testing, and the brief does not say whether the exit interview or the chat reply holds the answers; the genre is also left open, so the choice of stealth was mine.\\\",\\n \\\"Keeping every listed feature complete at once (attract, hub, glyphs, touch notice, About, save-free settings) with no stubs in one session.\\\",\\n \\\"A gamepad test: I had no controller, so the PlayStation and Xbox prompts and the axis inversion were checked only through the keyboard path and the settings flags.\\\",\\n]\\nabout = open('src/about.js').read()\\nold_t = \\\"['TESTING FEEDBACK', 'Testing feedback is in the chat reply and in exit-interview.json.'],\\\"\\nold_e = \\\"['ENGINE FEEDBACK', 'Engine feedback is in the chat reply and in exit-interview.json.'],\\\"\\nold_p = \\\"['PROMPT FEEDBACK', 'Prompt feedback is in the chat reply and in exit-interview.json.']\\\"\\nfor o in (old_t, old_e, old_p): assert about.count(o)==1, o\\ndef block(name, items):\\n    return \\\"['%s', %s]\\\" % (name, json.dumps(' '.join(f'{i+1}. {t}' for i,t in enumerate(items)), ensure_ascii=True))\\nabout = about.replace(old_t, block('TESTING FEEDBACK', TEST)+',').replace(old_e, block('ENGINE FEEDBACK', ENG)+',').replace(old_p, block('PROMPT FEEDBACK', PROMPT))\\nopen('src/about.js','w').write(about)\\nex = {\\n \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n   \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-02 18:58\\\",\\n   \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Wire (2002-2008)\\\",\\n   \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Stealth and investigation, with a shift clock\\\",\\n   \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Threequarter, switchable to topdown and iso\\\",\\n   \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge engine v0.85.1 (full build, bundled into one HTML file); AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.3.0 (session.js, unmodified)\\\",\\n   \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's pixel style with night lighting, the engine's pixel title font, and a Baltimore-block tileset\\\",\\n   \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine's Humanoid rigs and their poses\\\",\\n   \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Music, sound effects and voice written in code: chip-synth music, effects, and a gruff synth blip per letter (no sound files)\\\",\\n   \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub parallel round, 1 to 4 players; each copy reports its score\\\",\\n   \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Node suite (36 checks, including a full scripted playthrough), a Chromium run of the built file, the AI Hub harness with 2 and 4 players, and a WebKit viewport matrix (phone, tablet, desktop)\\\",\\n   \\\"research\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n   \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\",\\n   \\\"model\\\": \\\"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\",\\n   \\\"usage\\\": \\\"unknown\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"testingFeedback\\\": TEST,\\n \\\"engineFeedback\\\": ENG,\\n \\\"promptFeedback\\\": PROMPT,\\n \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n   \\\"name\\\": \\\"Wire on the Corner\\\",\\n   \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"One shift. Fayette & Monroe.\\\",\\n   \\\"description\\\": \\\"A plainclothes detective has one night to make a case on a Baltimore corner: tune the pole, talk to the people who know, stay out of the lookouts' sight, and bring the paper to the lieutenant.\\\",\\n   \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n   \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Stealth\\\",\\n   \\\"source\\\": \\\"The Wire (2002-2008)\\\",\\n   \\\"series\\\": \\\"The Wire\\\",\\n   \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n   \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or arrows walk, dash runs, confirm interacts and tunes, click to walk\\\",\\n   \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"pixel art\\\", \\\"top-down\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"exploration\\\"]\\n }\\n}\\njson.dump(ex, open('../exit-interview.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\\nprint('json ok', len(TEST), len(ENG), len(PROMPT))\\nEOF\\npython3 -c \\\"import json;d=json.load(open('/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-185845__x22cc1b/work/exit-interview.json'));print(sorted(d.keys()), len(d['testingFeedback']), len(d['engineFeedback']), len(d['promptFeedback']))\\\" && node build/build.mjs && node test/test.mjs | tail -1 && node -e \\\"1\\\" && cp ../WireOnTheCorner-TheWire-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261102-185845.html /tmp/wire-serve/ && cd /tmp/wire-shots && timeout 400 python3 hub_check.py 2 2>&1 | head -1 && grep -c \\\"TODO\\\\|placeholder\\\\|stub\\\" /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-185845__x22cc1b/work/WireOnTheCorner-TheWire-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261102-185845/src/*.js; pkill -f \\\"http.server 8123\\\"; echo done\",\"description\":\"Write feedback into About and exit-interview.json; final rebuild and checks\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1408,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":233462,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1408,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4accd6